---
# Same pagination trick as home.njk / contract.njk.
pagination:
  data: pages.schedule.locales
  size: 1
  alias: locale
permalink: "{{ locale.permalink }}"
---
{#
  TAQATHON - SCHEDULE PAGE TEMPLATE (src/pages/schedule.njk)
  ------------------------------------------------------------
  Workshop + key-dates table. Every row is data (see
  src/_data/copy/schedule.ar.json / schedule.en.json) rendered through
  two {% for %} loops below, rather than 9 hand-typed <tr> blocks.

  TO CUSTOMIZE:
    - Add/remove/reorder a workshop or key date → edit the "workshops"
      or "keyDates" arrays in the copy JSON files, NOT this file. A row
      with "action": null renders with an empty action cell (some
      events just don't have a join link).
    - Table headers, section headings → same copy JSON files.

  CLEANED UP DURING MIGRATION (zero visual effect, just removing dead
  weight found while transcribing the original pages):
    - Both original pages defined CSS custom properties --row-border
      and --section-bg that were never actually used anywhere else in
      either stylesheet. Dropped.
    - The Arabic page's <style> block re-declared the exact same
      scrollbar-hiding and sticky-footer rules already present in
      assets/common.css (word for word) — harmless duplication, not
      carried forward.
    - Both original pages had a stray, unmatched closing </a> tag sitting
      in an empty table cell (browsers silently ignore it) — on
      DIFFERENT rows in each language, suggesting leftover copy-paste
      debris rather than anything intentional. Not carried forward.
    - The Arabic Closing Ceremony row had a trailing <br> with nothing
      after it in the time cell (likely a deleted second line). Dropped.
    - .icon-circle i had two different single-property overrides in the
      two languages (Arabic: line-height:1 only: English: font-size only,
      which was already redundant since .icon-circle itself sets that
      size and icons inherit it). Unified to line-height:1 for both,
      since that's the one override that actually does something.
    - Icon margin utility classes: unlike Home/Contract (which used
      "ms-1" for Arabic icons, "me-1" for English), this page's ORIGINAL
      Arabic version actually used "me-1" almost everywhere already —
      except one single row (the Closing Ceremony's location icon),
      which used "ms-1", breaking its own page's pattern. Normalized
      the whole page to "me-1" (its own majority convention) rather
      than importing Home/Contract's convention or preserving a likely
      one-off typo.
    - The Arabic Closing Ceremony link opened with target="_blank" but
      no rel="noopener" (the English version had it). Adding
      rel="noopener" is a real, if minor, security improvement — it
      stops the newly-opened tab from being able to reach back and
      manipulate this page via window.opener — so it's applied to both
      languages now via one shared {% if k.action.external %} check,
      rather than left missing on the Arabic side.
#}
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}
{% block pageStyle %}
.icon-circle i{ line-height:1; }

.table thead th{
  color:#6b7785;
  font-weight:600;
}
.section-row td{
  background:#f2f6fb;
  font-weight:600;
  color:#17324a;
}
.table tbody tr.workshop-row td{ background:#ecfdf5; }
.table tbody tr.keydate-row td{ background:#eef6ff; }

.section-kicker{
  display:inline-flex;
  align-items:center;
  gap:.5rem;
  font-size:.9rem;
  color:#3664a3;
  text-transform:uppercase;
}
.k-dot{
  width:8px;
  height:8px;
  border-radius:999px;
  background:var(--brand-blue);
  box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(0,125,253,.12);
}

.btn-join{
  border-color:var(--brand-green);
  color:#0a7b60;
  background:#f4fffb;
}
.btn-join:hover{
  background:var(--brand-green);
  color:#fff;
  border-color:var(--brand-green);
}

{#
  work-title font differs meaningfully by language (Cairo for Arabic
  vs a Poppins-led Latin stack for English), and even the font-weight
  differs (700 vs 600) — real, deliberate-looking differences, so both
  come from data rather than a shared value.

  workTitleFontFamily uses "| safe" because it contains a single-quote
  character ('Cairo'). Without it, Nunjucks's default HTML-escaping
  turns that quote into its numeric character-entity form — and just
  like the <script>-tag issue documented in contract.njk, text inside
  a <style> tag is never HTML-entity-decoded by the browser either. The
  escaped quote would make the CSS parser treat "Cairo" as an unknown,
  literally-entity-encoded font name and silently fall back to plain
  sans-serif instead of loading the actual Cairo font — caught here
  the same way the script-tag version was caught on the Contract page:
  by diffing the build output against the live file before shipping.
#}
.table td .work-title{
  font-family:{{ locale.content.workTitleFontFamily | safe }} !important;
  font-weight:{{ locale.content.workTitleFontWeight }} !important;
}
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<main class="py-5">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:980px;">

    <div class="text-center mb-4">
      <div class="icon-circle mx-auto mb-3"><i class="bi {{ locale.content.hero.icon }}"></i></div>
      <h5 class="mb-1 {{ locale.content.hero.headingClass }}">{{ locale.content.hero.heading }}</h5>
      <div style="height: 20px;"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="card card-lite rounded-2xl shadow-soft">
      <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="table align-middle mb-0">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>{{ locale.content.tableHeaders.item }}</th>
              <th>{{ locale.content.tableHeaders.date }}</th>
              <th>{{ locale.content.tableHeaders.time }}</th>
              <th style="min-width:180px;">{{ locale.content.tableHeaders.action }}</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>

            <!-- Workshops -->
            <tr class="section-row">
              <td colspan="4">
                <span class="section-kicker">
                  <span class="k-dot"></span> {{ locale.content.workshopsHeading }}
                </span>
              </td>
            </tr>

            {% for w in locale.content.workshops %}
            <tr class="workshop-row">
              <td>
                <div class="work-title">{{ w.title }}</div>
                <div class="small text-secondary">{{ w.presenter }}</div>
              </td>
              <td>{{ w.date }}</td>
              <td>{{ w.time }}</td>
              <td>
                <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-success btn-join" href="{{ w.action.href }}">
                  <i class="bi {{ w.action.icon }} {{ locale.content.iconMarginClass }}"></i> {{ w.action.label }}
                </a>
              </td>
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}

            <!-- Key Dates -->
            <tr class="section-row">
              <td colspan="4">
                <span class="section-kicker">
                  <span class="k-dot"></span> {{ locale.content.keyDatesHeading }}
                </span>
              </td>
            </tr>

            {% for k in locale.content.keyDates %}
            <tr class="keydate-row">
              <td><div class="work-title">{{ k.title }}</div></td>
              <td>{{ k.date }}</td>
              <td>{{ k.time }}</td>
              <td>
                {% if k.action %}
                <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-success btn-join" href="{{ k.action.href }}"{% if k.action.external %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>
                  <i class="bi {{ k.action.icon }} {{ locale.content.iconMarginClass }}"></i> {{ k.action.label }}
                </a>
                {% endif %}
              </td>
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}

          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
{% endblock %}
